          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            6+1 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
          %h2#RelationToOtherBranes Relation to other branes
          %h3#to_the_kkmonopole_in_mtheory To the KK-monopole in M-theory
          %p
            The lift of the D6 to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            there (
            %a{:href => "#Townsend95"}> Townsend 95
            ).
          %p
            One way to understand this is as follows: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            of the M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-brane
            degree-2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-duality
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge dual
            of the D6-brane degree-8 field strength. Now given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            after removing the locus of the monopole where the circle-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            degenerates (as in the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            argument) it is a non-degenerated circle bundle such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integral
            of the 2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            surrounding the singular locus is non-trivial. By the usual yoga of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric-magnetic+duality"} electric-magnetic duality
            this integral measures the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+flux"} magnetic flux
            of a D6-brane sitting at the singular locus. For more on this see at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Kaluza-Klein+monopole#RelationToTheD6Brane"} Kaluza-Klein monopole – Relation to the D6-brane
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
          %h3#to_d7branes To D7-branes
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            of the D6 branes is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-brane"} D7-brane
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
          %h3#bound_states Bound states
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"}> bound states
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersections"} brane intersections
            involving D6-branes:
